S644 Vieta-perfect aliquot carriers
===================================

Carrier identities
------------------
Triangular pair count: A = C(n,2)
Vieta/discriminant carrier: 8A + 1 = (2n - 1)^2
LRC shell clock: C = 2n - 1 = sqrt(8A + 1)
Aliquot map: s(A) = sigma(A) - A, the sum of proper divisors

The unique doubled/tripled-prime crossing
-----------------------------------------
Search n<= 20000: [6]
Proof: if 2p = 3q with p,q prime, then 3 divides p, so p=3.
Then 6 = 3q, hence q=2 and the common value is 6.
The same 6 is the unique distinct product-sum resonance:
  6 = 2*3 = 1+2+3 = 1*2*3
  sigma(6)=12, aliquot(6)=6, 8*6+1=49=7^2

Even perfect numbers as triangular fixed controls
-------------------------------------------------
Euclid-Euler rows with Mersenne prime M=2^p-1:
  p   M        n=2^p     A=C(n,2)        shell      s(A)
  2   3        4         6               7          6
  3   7        8         28              15         28
  5   31       32        496             63         496
  7   127      128       8128            255        8128
  13  8191     8192      33550336        16383      33550336
  17  131071   131072    8589869056      262143     8589869056
  19  524287   524288    137438691328    1048575    137438691328
Here s(A)=A, so perfect numbers are fixed points of the aliquot
map inside the same triangular/Vieta carrier used by LRC clocks.

LRC triangular rows and aliquot shadows
--------------------------------------
  n    A=C(n,2)   factor(A)        shell=2n-1   s(A)   class
  4    6          2*3              7            6      perfect
  6    15         3*5              11           9      deficient
  8    28         2^2*7            15           28     perfect
  10   45         3^2*5            19           33     deficient
  12   66         2*3*11           23           78     abundant
  14   91         7*13             27           21     deficient  <== n=14 gives s(91)=21
  16   120        2^3*3*5          31           240    abundant
  18   153        3^2*17           35           81     deficient
  20   190        2*5*19           39           170    deficient
  21   210        2*3*5*7          41           366    abundant
  22   231        3*7*11           43           153    deficient
  32   496        2^4*31           63           496    perfect
  38   703        19*37            75           57     deficient
  62   1891       31*61            123          93     deficient
  128  8128       2^6*127          255          8128   perfect

Key row:
  C(14,2) = 91 = 7*13
  s(91) = 21
  sqrt(8*91+1) = 27 = 2*14-1
So 21 is an exact divisor-sum shadow of the n=14 pair-count carrier.

Semiprime family n=2p with 2p-1 prime
-------------------------------------
If p and q=2p-1 are prime, then C(2p,2)=p*q and
  s(C(2p,2)) = 1 + p + q = 3p.
This is a whole family where the triangular pair count casts a
tripled-prime aliquot shadow.

  p    q=2p-1   n=2p   A=C(n,2)   s(A)=3p   diagonal packet
  2    3        4      6           6         (2p,3p)=(4,6)
  3    5        6      15          9         (2p,3p)=(6,9)
  7    13       14     91          21        (2p,3p)=(14,21)  <== p=7 gives n=14, shadow 21
  19   37       38     703         57        (2p,3p)=(38,57)
  31   61       62     1891        93        (2p,3p)=(62,93)
  37   73       74     2701        111       (2p,3p)=(74,111)
  79   157      158    12403       237       (2p,3p)=(158,237)
  97   193      194    18721       291       (2p,3p)=(194,291)
  139  277      278    38503       417       (2p,3p)=(278,417)
  157  313      314    49141       471       (2p,3p)=(314,471)
  199  397      398    79003       597       (2p,3p)=(398,597)
  211  421      422    88831       633       (2p,3p)=(422,633)

Vieta/discriminant examples
---------------------------
  A=6     factor=2*3          8A+1=49      sqrt=7    n=4    s(A)=6
  A=15    factor=3*5          8A+1=121     sqrt=11   n=6    s(A)=9
  A=28    factor=2^2*7        8A+1=225     sqrt=15   n=8    s(A)=28
  A=91    factor=7*13         8A+1=729     sqrt=27   n=14   s(A)=21
  A=231   factor=3*7*11       8A+1=1849    sqrt=43   n=22   s(A)=153
  A=496   factor=2^4*31       8A+1=3969    sqrt=63   n=32   s(A)=496
  A=703   factor=19*37        8A+1=5625    sqrt=75   n=38   s(A)=57
  A=8128  factor=2^6*127      8A+1=65025   sqrt=255  n=128  s(A)=8128

This is the Vieta carrier x^2+x-2A=0.  For A=C(n,2),
the positive root is x=n-1 and the discriminant root is 2n-1.

